      "id": "claim_ce259eb9912a4567bdf1a11f9a00dd53",
      "statement": "The workflow push guard keys human approval by fingerprint in per-thread workflow_push_approvals metadata: an approved fingerprint causes the push to be rewritten to a safe explicit head_sha:refs/heads/branch refspec and allowed, while a non-approved fingerprint blocks the push with WorkflowPushApprovalRequired, records a pending approval, and posts a one-time Slack approval message; any further workflow-file change yields a new fingerprint requiring fresh approval.",
